# The API's configuration is not here: it is backend/.env, from backend/.env.example (passkeys,
# sessions, invites, push, mail, media limits, the database). See backend/README.md and
# docs/SELF_HOSTING.md. This file held the Node API's variables until it was retired (CHW-301).
#
# What is left at the root is for developers only.

# ── Hevy map regeneration ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not used by the running app. End users paste their own key in Settings →
# Import from Hevy. Set this only to regenerate frontend/src/lib/hevy-id-map.js:
#
#   HEVY_API_KEY=
#   node scripts/build-hevy-id-map.mjs
